# Pages serves a real file when one matches; these rules only apply when none does.
#
# A missing hashed asset must 404. By default the SPA fallback answered it with
# index.html as 200 text/html, and because assets carry max-age=14400 browsers
# then cached an HTML document under a .css/.js URL for four hours. That is what
# blanked the Tables page: the route's dynamic import got HTML instead of a
# stylesheet and rejected. A 404 is not cached that way and fails loudly.
/assets/*  /404.html  404

# Everything else is client-side routing.
/*  /index.html  200
